{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794759528,"nonce":"HuSVTuGMtCOURJbNVmkM8VxjJZo=","title":"A scroll container that was never painted makes the page stale, so every drawn frame is a full paint","message":"`RenderTree::scroll_off_rows_changed` (d658ade0, 2026-11-12) treated a scroll container with no recorded paint as stale. A container is recorded when the walker paints it, so one that is culled, hidden or inside a closed overlay never is. The window reads `scroll_paint_stale()` in `try_fast_paint` (present.rs: `scroll_blocks_fast`), so a page with any such container never takes the cache: every frame that is drawn is a full paint.\n\nThe cn demo has several (code blocks, lists, the calendar, select and combobox lists). In a headless session of the real demo, `scroll_paint_stale()` was true at rest and is false with the fix (tools/blinc-bench, example cn_demo_costs).\n\nFixed by treating a container with no paint as having nothing stale. Tests: scroll_paint_stale in blinc_recorder (the first fails without the fix).\n\nNot measured in a window: the headless session computes its own fast-path flag and still paints in full for another reason (its epoch check), so the frame times it prints do not show the saving. A window of the cn demo, scrolled, is the check.\n\nLabels: bug, perf, area:layout.","files":null}]}